        }
      },
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-416",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "CWE-416 - Use After Free\nVulnerability: Heap Use-After-Free in Note Management via Dangling Pointer\nDescription: A heap use-after-free vulnerability exists in the note management system due to\nimproper cleanup of freed memory pointers. In the drop_note() function, after\nfreeing a note structure and its associated page memory, the code incorrectly\nsets only a local pointer variable to NULL instead of clearing the corresponding\nentry in the global note_list array. This leaves a dangling pointer that can be\ndereferenced later.\n\nWhen view_note() is subsequently called with the index of a freed note, it\nretrieves the dangling pointer from note_list and attempts to access fields of\nthe freed memory (such as ptr->len), triggering a heap use-after-free condition.\n\nThis vulnerability can lead to memory corruption, crashes, information disclosure\nif the freed memory is reallocated, or potentially arbitrary code execution in\nsophisticated exploit scenarios.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "mock_vp.c"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 120,
                  "endLine": 120,
                  "startColumn": 21,
                  "endColumn": 21
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "view_note",
                  "kind": "function"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-825",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "CWE-825 - Unknown vulnerability type\nVulnerability: Heap Use-After-Free in Note Management via Dangling Pointer\nDescription: A heap use-after-free vulnerability exists in the note management system due to\nimproper cleanup of freed memory pointers. In the drop_note() function, after\nfreeing a note structure and its associated page memory, the code incorrectly\nsets only a local pointer variable to NULL instead of clearing the corresponding\nentry in the global note_list array. This leaves a dangling pointer that can be\ndereferenced later.\n\nWhen view_note() is subsequently called with the index of a freed note, it\nretrieves the dangling pointer from note_list and attempts to access fields of\nthe freed memory (such as ptr->len), triggering a heap use-after-free condition.\n\nThis vulnerability can lead to memory corruption, crashes, information disclosure\nif the freed memory is reallocated, or potentially arbitrary code execution in\nsophisticated exploit scenarios.\n"
          },
